Hi all,

This here's the initial announcement that, for our fifth year, the
/dev/null/nethack Tournament will begin at midnight on Halloween (California
time).  It will run through the entire month of November.

There is a countdown timer on the Tournament site at
<http://nethack.devnull.net>.

We are currently looking for folks to volunteer to run game servers for this
year.  You can review the game server software and requirements at
<http://nethack.devnull.net/software.html>.  Please email us at the address
listed on the web page if you're interested.

We have in the past implemented one new major feature per year in the
Tournament code (last year's being the new Most Unique Deaths trophy).  My
brother Matt, who originally suggested holding an annual NetHack tournament and
the author of much of our Tournament system, is back from Peru and will be
working on the Tournament again this year so we may be able to get time to do
another project (personally, my project will be to catch up on the _huge_
trophy backlog).  If anyone has suggestions for what they'd like to see, let us
know.

See you in a few weeks.  ;-)

Cheers,
-robin

(Traditional note for past winners:  There are still many trophies from
